WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:10.316
Nine walls stand in a row, and you must pick the pair that holds the most water.

00:10.316 --> 00:14.700
Trying every pair means n² checks.

00:15.000 --> 00:27.572
Instead, start with the widest container: the first and last walls.

00:27.572 --> 00:31.700
Measure what it holds.

00:32.000 --> 00:40.454
The shorter wall is the limit, so move it inward.

00:40.454 --> 00:47.700
The taller wall never needs to move first.

00:48.000 --> 00:56.495
Each wall moves once, so one pass finds the best: 49.

00:56.495 --> 00:59.700
That’s two pointers.

